        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agent): return data URIs for workspace-relative identity card avatars (#97602)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`agent.identity.get` returned inline data URIs for workspace-relative avatars, but the **Control UI Personal card** is initialized from the **bootstrap config** (`control-ui-config.json`), which still mapped workspace avatars through `resolveAssistantAvatarUrl` to the auth-gated `/avatar/<agentId>` route. An `<img>` tag cannot carry a Bearer header, so the linked Personal-card 401/broken-image symptom persisted despite the RPC fix.\n\nThis PR consolidates the workspace-safe avatar reader into **one shared, gateway-internal helper** (`readLocalAvatarDataUrl` in `session-utils.ts`) and uses it in **both** projections — `agent.identity.get` and the bootstrap config handler — so identity and bootstrap produce identical inline data URIs. Remote HTTP URLs, existing data URLs, text fallbacks, and the `/avatar/<agentId>` HTTP endpoint are unchanged.\n\nThe helper is **not** re-exported on the Plugin SDK surface (`session-utils.ts` is gateway-internal; the `identity-avatar` barrel does not re-export it). The workspace root is canonicalised with `realpathSync` to keep the containment check correct for symlinked workspaces.\n\nFixes #97602.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Personal card in Control UI showed a broken avatar image because its avatar comes from the bootstrap config, not from `agent.identity.get`:\n- UI chat avatar → `agent.identity.get` (already fixed in the first revision).\n- **Config Personal card** → `appConfig.assistantIdentity.avatar` → bootstrap `control-ui-config.json` → `/avatar/<agentId>` (auth-gated → `<img>` 401). **This PR fixes this path.**\n\nGiven a workspace with an avatar file `avatar.png`:\n- **Before**: bootstrap `assistantAvatar` = `/avatar/main` (route URL → `<img>` 401)\n- **After**: bootstrap `assistantAvatar` = `data:image/png;base64,...` (inline → renders)\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClawSweeper's P1: the earlier fix covered only `agent.identity.get`, leaving the bootstrap Personal-card path emitting the protected route. Rather than duplicate a third avatar reader, this revision lands **one canonical projection**:\n1. `readLocalAvatarDataUrl(filePath, workspaceDir)` moves from `agent.ts` into `session-utils.ts` (exported gateway-internal, off the SDK barrel).\n2. `agent.identity.get` imports the shared helper (behaviour unchanged).\n3. The bootstrap config handler resolves the avatar via the same `resolveAgentAvatar(...)` and, when `kind === \"local\"`, inlines the file with the shared helper before `resolveAssistantAvatarUrl` (which passes data URIs through untouched). On any failure it falls back to the route URL.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/gateway/session-utils.ts`: add exported gateway-internal `readLocalAvatarDataUrl` (shared reader).\n- `src/gateway/server-methods/agent.ts`: import the shared helper; remove the now-duplicated private copy and its now-unused imports.\n- `src/gateway/control-ui.ts`: inline workspace-local avatars as data URIs in the bootstrap config response.\n- `src/gateway/control-ui.http.test.ts`: bootstrap-config regression test asserting a workspace-local avatar is returned as a data URI (not `/avatar/main`).\n\n## Evidence\n\n**1. Bootstrap regression test (new) + identity/list regressions — all green**\n\n```\nnode vitest run src/gateway/control-ui.http.test.ts \\\n  src/gateway/server-methods/agent.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/identity-avatar.test.ts \\\n  src/gateway/session-utils.test.ts -t \"avatar|identity\"\n\nTest Files  10 passed (10)\n     Tests  77 passed | 898 skipped (975)\n```\n\nThe new test `inlines a workspace-local assistant avatar as a data URI in bootstrap config (#97602)` fails on the pre-fix bootstrap handler and passes after.\n\n**2. Real behavior proof — standalone harness driving the real `handleControlUiHttpRequest` bootstrap path**\n\nA standalone script (not a committed test) creates a real workspace with a real `avatar.png`, invokes the production bootstrap-config handler, and prints the `assistantAvatar` from the actual JSON response body:\n\n```\n========== BEFORE (PR head control-ui.ts) ==========\nhandled: true\nassistantAvatar (first 48 chars): \"/avatar/main\"\nstartsWith 'data:image/png;base64,' -> false\ncontains '/avatar/main' (broken auth-gated route) -> true\n\n========== AFTER (fix) ==========\nhandled: true\nassistantAvatar (first 48 chars): \"data:image/png;base64,YXZhdGFyLWJ5dGVzCg==\"\nstartsWith 'data:image/png;base64,' -> true\ncontains '/avatar/main' (broken auth-gated route) -> false\n```\n\n**3. Lint:** `oxlint` on the three changed source files — clean (exit 0).\n\n## AI-assisted\n\nThis PR was AI-assisted (Claude Code).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
